      "hints": [
        "At $P$, use $\\overrightarrow{PX}$ (or $\\overrightarrow{XP}$) and $\\overrightarrow{PO}$ (or $\\overrightarrow{OP}$).",
        "Set the dot product to zero and solve the resulting quadratic."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{XP}=-4\\mathbf{i}+(p-5)\\mathbf{j}+2\\mathbf{k}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OP}=p\\mathbf{j}+2\\mathbf{k}$.",
        "Perpendicularity gives $\\overrightarrow{XP}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{OP}=p(p-5)+4=0$. Hence $(p-1)(p-4)=0$ and $p=1$ or $p=4$."
      ],
